WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.480
It's just a mess, there’s s*** everywhere

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.020
It's just a mess out here.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.120
Where is the poorest, dirtiest,

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.300
most depressing slum in the world?

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.300
In Haiti?

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.320
India?

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.340
Africa?

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.500
Is that what this is?

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.560
No.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.880
I'm in America.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.760
One of the richest parts of America.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.380
Highest rents in all of America.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.420
This is San Francisco today.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.847
Encampments of street people

00:00:23.847 --> 00:00:24.800
everywhere.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.300
Some pitch tents,

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.100
planning to stay a long time.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.720
Some have mental problems.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.800
Vampires are real and I’m paranoid as all hell.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.840
Other street people complain about them.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.910
They run around and they shout at themselves.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.160
They make it bad for people like us

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.500
that hang out with a sign.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.180
Some people shoot up in plain sight.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:50.500
It’s nasty, seeing somebody actually shoot up drugs,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.420
like right there.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.180
The police don’t do anything about it.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.880
They’ll get somebody for drinking a beer,

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.320
but they’ll walk right past

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.680
people using needles.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.720
Every day in San Francisco,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.260
an average of 85 cars are broken into.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.950
They're called smash and grabs.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.400
Inside Edition left things in a car

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.860
to test how long they'd last.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:13.820
Not long.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.320
Watch as these Bonnie and Clyde wannabes

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.000
stroll up and peer inside our car.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.440
They wait here for the sidewalk to clear.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.440
Then the thief throws up his hood.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:26.440
There he goes, he just broke in.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:26.940
Hey, what's going on?

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:27.440
Hey, guys!

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.040
Good.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:28.700
Everything good today?

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.540
Yeah!

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:32.640
Since store owners can’t rely on city cops to

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.660
deal with the masses of homeless,

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.600
some hire private police to patrol around their stores.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.560
Cody Clements works this neighborhood.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.620
A lot of times

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.160
because somebody who pays for our service

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.680
call and says, "Hey, there's

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.200
a homeless group of people setting up a camp

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.380
in front of my business or my residence.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.540
Can you come, ask them to move?"

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.240
There used to be hundreds of private cops like Cody.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.140
But then San Francisco's police

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.750
union complained.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.380
Now there are fewer than 10 left.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.380
Can I just have you guys stand up for me?

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.960
Cody offers help to people living on the streets,

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.080
but most turn it down.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.040
Do you need any type of homeless outreach services

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:09.560
or anything?

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.360
San Francisco is generous.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.440
It offers street people food stamps,

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.587
free shelter,

00:02:16.587 --> 00:02:17.856
train tickets,

00:02:17.856 --> 00:02:19.850
and $70/month in cash.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.460
I don't use any resources,

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.440
but they're always offering resources.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.120
San Francisco's just a good place to hang out.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:26.657
Like many,

00:02:26.657 --> 00:02:28.590
these two come here from out of town.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:29.810
Do you like the lifestyle?

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.040
Of course I do.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.860
As you just heard, they love the freedom

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.320
of not having to follow the rules.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.878
So the homeless stay on the streets and every day,

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.440
new people arrive.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.760
Some residents want the city to get tougher

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.700
with people living on the streets.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.400
Get them to the point

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.820
where they have to make a decision

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.300
between jail and rehab.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.240
And there's a way we can do that.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.020
Other cities do it, but for some reason,

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.020
San Francisco doesn't have the political will to.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.020
San Francisco's politicians have promised

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.960
to fix the homeless problem.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.160
They've promised that for decades.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:02.260
If there is a problem involving housing or homelessness,

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.720
you gotta do something about it.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.140
As part of the city's program,

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.740
the homeless were to be temporarily housed in hotels.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.500
A thousands units right here in the Tenderloin.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:15.400
We have already moved 6,860 human beings.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.080
So we need to fund programs like Homeward Bound.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.760
But the extra funding hasn’t worked.

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:23.880
The number of street people has grown most every year.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.209
Hey officer!

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:27.240
One reason is that even if some of these people

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.960
wanted to get off the street,

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.540
to rent an apartment,

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.020
there aren't many apartments available.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.840
Most of San Francisco looks like this.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.160
Three story buildings,

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:39.340
maybe two apartments per building.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.240
You can't add onto that.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.540
It's illegal.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.863
Because of that,

00:03:43.863 --> 00:03:46.840
housing that exists costs a fortune.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.860
This doesn't look like an expensive neighborhood,

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.180
but these houses sell for millions of dollars?

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.620
Millions of dollars.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.500
What if I come in,

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.940
and I bought this property,

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:56.580
and I want to put up an apartment building

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.160
that would house a bunch of people?

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.260
Yeah, too bad.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.840
Laura’s Foote’s non-profit runs ads that

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.020
try to convince residents to allow bigger buildings,

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:08.760
to say YIMBY, “Yes In My Backyard”.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.460
But good luck with that.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.600
Even in liberal San Francisco,

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.099
people don’t want that.

00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:15.099
I would hate it.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.180
I would hate it.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.560
I think it'd be really congested.

00:04:18.569 --> 00:04:20.520
Where will people live?

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.860
I'm not sure.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.240
You're a builder, go build stuff.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.480
Let me build.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.880
John Dennis has been trying to replace this

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.180
grimy old building.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:31.830
This has been a defunct meatpacking plant.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.860
It's been empty for at least 15 years.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.310
He wants to turn this

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:37.000
into this,

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.380
which would house 60 people.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:40.940
But it’s taken 4 years

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.260
just to get permission to build.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.560
And all that time, we're paying property taxes,

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.660
and we're paying for maintenance of the building.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:50.260
People in San Francisco often claim to be

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.380
all about helping the poor.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.700
But their policies make life tougher for the poor.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.939
What's your next project in San Francisco?

00:04:57.939 --> 00:04:59.509
No more projects in San Francisco.

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:00.000
I'm done.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.280
I'll never do another project here.

